{"id": "RT-science-genetics-gen-09", "body": {"t": "main", "a": {"class": "wrap", "id": "main-content"}, "c": [" ", " ", {"t": "p", "a": {"class": "kicker"}, "c": ["Science / Practical · GEN-09"]}, " ", {"t": "h1", "c": ["Family history and inheritance patterns"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-meta"}, "c": [{"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["Last updated 30 September 2026"]}, {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["GEN-09"]}]}, " ", {"t": "details", "a": {"class": "toc", "open": "true"}, "c": [{"t": "summary", "c": ["On this page"]}, {"t": "ol", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-mitochondrial-biology-can-explain"}, "c": ["What mitochondrial biology can explain"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-needs-distinguishing"}, "c": ["What needs distinguishing"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#inheritance-patterns-in-plain-english"}, "c": ["Inheritance patterns in plain English"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#how-to-collect-a-useful-family-history"}, "c": ["How to collect a useful family history"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-a-negative-family-history-does-and-does-not-mean"}, "c": ["What a negative family history does and does not mean"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-this-evidence-can-tell-us"}, "c": ["What this evidence can tell us"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#sources"}, "c": ["Sources"]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-body gen-article"}, "c": [" ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-mitochondrial-biology-can-explain"}, "c": ["What mitochondrial biology can explain"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["A good family history is one of the cheapest, most useful things you can give a clinician. It tells them which inheritance pattern to look for and which tests are worth requesting. ADHD clusters in families but does not follow a simple single-gene pattern. Some rare movement conditions do."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-needs-distinguishing", "class": "sec sec-misread"}, "c": ["What needs distinguishing"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["\"Nobody else in my family has it, so it cannot be genetic.\" Not so. A variant can arise for the first time in you (", {"t": "em", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-de-novo", "title": "New in a person, not inherited from either parent"}, "c": ["de novo"]}]}, "), sit silently in both parents (recessive), or show up weakly or not at all in relatives (reduced ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-penetrance", "title": "The share of carriers who develop the condition. \"Reduced penetrance\" means some carriers never do"}, "c": ["penetrance"]}, "). Relatives may also be undiagnosed, especially in older generations."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "inheritance-patterns-in-plain-english"}, "c": ["Inheritance patterns in plain English"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "table-wrap", "role": "region", "aria-label": "Table"}, "c": [{"t": "table", "c": [{"t": "thead", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Pattern"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["What it looks like in a family"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Example in this series"]}]}]}, {"t": "tbody", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Autosomal dominant"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["One changed copy is enough. Can appear in every generation"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Dominant GCH1 deficiency, the commonest ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-dopa-responsive-dystonia", "title": "A group of conditions, often involving the GCH1 or TH genes, in which symptoms improve markedly with low-dose levodopa"}, "c": ["dopa-responsive dystonia"]}, " form ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Autosomal recessive"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Two changed copies needed. Parents usually unaffected carriers. Often skips generations"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Recessive GCH1 deficiency ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-2", "aria-label": "Source 2"}, "c": ["2"]}, "]"]}, "; most reported SPG7-related disease (", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "hold"}, "c": ["not yet verified"]}, ")"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["X-linked"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Passed on the X chromosome. Affects males more obviously"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Not a main pattern in this series"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["De novo"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["New in the affected person, absent in both parents"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Rare damaging variants in ADHD ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-3", "aria-label": "Source 3"}, "c": ["3"]}, "]"]}]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Polygenic (many small effects)"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Clusters in families with no clean pattern"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Typical ADHD ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-4", "aria-label": "Source 4"}, "c": ["4"]}, "]"]}]}]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "h3", "a": {"id": "two-ideas-that-explain-missing-family-history"}, "c": ["Two ideas that explain \"missing\" family history"]}, " ", {"t": "ul", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Reduced penetrance."]}, " Some carriers never develop symptoms. In the dominant GCH1 form, symptoms are more common in females, and most asymptomatic adult carriers were male ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}, ". A parent can carry the variant while seeming unaffected."]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Variable expressivity."]}, " Carriers of the same variant can be mildly or severely affected, or affected in different ways."]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "how-to-collect-a-useful-family-history"}, "c": ["How to collect a useful family history"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["Aim for three generations: you, parents, siblings, grandparents, aunts, uncles, cousins and children. For each person, note the following."]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "table-wrap", "role": "region", "aria-label": "Table"}, "c": [{"t": "table", "c": [{"t": "thead", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Question"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Why it helps"]}]}]}, {"t": "tbody", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Relationship and age, or age at death"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Places them on the tree"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Any diagnosed condition, and at what age it started"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Age of onset separates inheritance patterns"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Walking, stiffness, tremor, falls, \"clumsy\" or \"tight\" legs; symptoms that vary through the day"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Flags movement disorders, including dopa-responsive types"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["ADHD, autism, dyslexia, learning difficulties, or \"never diagnosed but obviously\""]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Shows neurodevelopmental clustering"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Any genetic tests and their results"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Avoids repeating work"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Parents who are blood relatives, or shared ancestry or region"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Raises the chance of recessive conditions"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Response to medicines (what helped, what made things worse)"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Can echo across relatives"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Early deaths, and causes"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["May reveal undiagnosed conditions"]}]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Keep it factual."]}, " Record what is known and mark guesses as guesses. A clinician can work with \"uncle, walked stiffly from his thirties, never diagnosed\"."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-a-negative-family-history-does-and-does-not-mean"}, "c": ["What a negative family history does and does not mean"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["It lowers the odds of some dominant conditions but does not exclude recessive, de novo or reduced-penetrance conditions, nor relatives' undiagnosed disease. Clinicians weigh it alongside examination and tests."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-this-evidence-can-tell-us", "class": "sec sec-limit"}, "c": ["What this evidence can tell us"]}, " ", {"t": "ul", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": ["This page explains patterns; it does not say what pattern any family has."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["The reduced-penetrance statement applies to dominant GCH1 deficiency as reported in the MDSGene review ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}, ". Other conditions differ."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["ADHD is not inherited like a single-gene condition ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-4", "aria-label": "Source 4"}, "c": ["4"]}, "]"]}, "."]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "sources", "class": "sec sec-src"}, "c": ["Sources"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["Bibliographic details checked against PubMed."]}, " ", {"t": "ol", "c": [{"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-1"}, "c": ["Weissbach A et al. Relationship of genotype, phenotype, and treatment in dopa-responsive dystonia: MDSGene review. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Mov Disord"]}, " 2022;37(2):237-252. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1002/mds.28874", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34908184/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["34908184"]}]}, {"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-2"}, "c": ["Novelli M et al. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Mov Disord Clin Pract"]}, " 2024;11(9):1072-1084. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1002/mdc3.14157", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39001623/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["39001623"]}]}, {"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-3"}, "c": ["Olfson E et al. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Nat Commun"]}, " 2024;15:5870. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-50247-7", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38997333/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["38997333"]}]}, {"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-4"}, "c": ["Faraone SV, Larsson H. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Mol Psychiatry"]}, " 2019;24(4):562-575. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41380-018-0070-0", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29892054/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["29892054"]}]}]}, " "]}, " ", {"t": "p", "a": {"class": "gloss-hint"}, "c": ["Underlined terms link to the ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/"}, "c": ["glossary"]}, "; hover or long-press for a quick definition."]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "nextbox"}, "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Useful next destination."]}, " ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-10/"}, "c": ["GEN-10"]}, ": Autism genetics in brief."]}, " ", {"t": "nav", "a": {"class": "gen-series", "aria-label": "Genetics series"}, "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/"}, "c": ["All genetics articles"]}, {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/"}, "c": ["Glossary"]}, {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/sources/numbers/"}, "c": ["Verified numbers"]}]}, " "]}}